tr_by=hand
why=pelt#49, ruling #113: with set -o autocd a name with no slash that command search finds nowhere and that names a directory (a child, a quoted name with a space, a name from a variable) runs cd -- NAME; the check is on the word as it stands, so cd then takes CDPATH as it always does (a directory both here and in CDPATH goes to CDPATH's, as bash; one only in CDPATH is not a directory here and stays not found, 127, as bash; zsh looks in cdpath too). bash 5.3 agrees on every row and writes cd -- NAME on standard error (black-box, notes/sh23-evidence/refs/base/bash-i-autocd/p02-bare, p10-cdpath). Written by hand from pelt trunk's answers to the explicit session (notes/sh23-evidence/handtr.py)
